We are now ready to define our first learning algorithm based on the \(\lambda\)-return: the _off-line \(\lambda\)-return algorithm_. As an off-line algorithm, it makes no changes to the weight vector during the episode. Then, at the end of the episode, a whole sequence of off-line updates are made according to our usual semi-gradient rule, using the \(\lambda\)-return as the target:

\[\mathbf{w}_{t+1}\doteq\mathbf{w}_{t}+\alpha\Big{[}G_{t}^{\lambda}-\hat{v}(S_{t },\!\mathbf{w}_{t})\Big{]}\nabla\hat{v}(S_{t},\!\mathbf{w}_{t}),\;\;\;t=0, \ldots,T-1. \tag{12.4}\]

